{"availability":"available","full":"yogthos/Matryoshka","name":"Matryoshka","description":"MCP server for token-efficient large document analysis via the use of REPL state","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":150,"forks":20,"created":"2026-01-12T17:23:41Z","updated":"2026-05-17T18:19:18Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["ai-assistant","document-analysis","llm","llm-tools","mcp","mcp-server","model-context-protocol"],"demo":"https://tree-sitter.github.io/tree-sitter/playground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:15:43.922Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:15:43.922Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:15:43.922Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":149,"forks":20},{"at":"2026-10-04T11:31:37.504Z","stars":149,"forks":20},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:31:32.125Z","stars":149,"forks":20},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:09:13.435Z","stars":150,"forks":20},{"at":"2026-10-11T07:24:26.089Z","stars":150,"forks":20},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:15:43.922Z","stars":150,"forks":20}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Process documents 100x larger than your LLM's context window—without vector databases or chunking heuristics."],"features":["The resource-limit features remain runRLM-only. The recursive primitives (rlmquery/rlmbatch) work in both paths — the MCP path spawns a child runRLMFromContent whose llmClient is the same sampling bridge as the parent,…","runRLM: children fan out concurrently via a worker pool capped at maxConcurrentSubcalls (default 4).","lattice-mcp: children run sequentially because the multi-turn suspension protocol can carry only one pending request at a time. Round-trip count is identical to the concurrent path (N children × M turns each); only…","Per-doc line numbers come back, so the LLM can cite \"doc 0 line 4, doc 2 line 2\" with confidence rather than inventing absolute offset